<section id="redeem" style={{ padding: "1rem 1rem 2.5rem", background: "var(--bg-secondary)" }}>
  <div class="container" style={{ maxWidth: "900px" }}>
    <span class="section-title">Redemption</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading">How to buy and redeem a Linux Foundation voucher</h2>
    <p style={{ color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.95rem", lineHeight: 1.75, margin: "0.75rem 0 1.25rem" }}>
      Udemy sells the voucher code; the Linux Foundation owns the certification and PSI delivers the exam. Buying and booking are two separate steps — do them in this order.
    </p>
    <ol style={{ margin: 0, paddingLeft: "1.3rem", color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.94rem", lineHeight: 1.9 }}>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Choose the right exam.</strong> CKA first for most people. CKS only after CKA is passed. CNPE if you already work on platform engineering.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Buy the voucher on Udemy.</strong> Use the official listing. The price is $311.50; coupons do not apply. The voucher is non-refundable, so buy only when you are ready to study.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Copy the code from My Learning → Certifications.</strong> Udemy also emails the code, but your account is the source of truth. Keep the purchase date — the 6-month redemption window starts then.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Redeem the code in the Linux Foundation My Portal.</strong> Sign in to your LF account, open the certification dashboard and redeem the voucher. Do this within 6 months of purchase.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Schedule through PSI.</strong> From the LF portal you are directed to PSI. Choose a date and time; Linux Foundation exams are online and remotely proctored only.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Run the system test and check your ID.</strong> You need a quiet room, a stable connection, a webcam, a microphone and a government ID. The name on your LF account must match the ID.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Take the exam within 12 months of redemption.</strong> If you fail the first attempt, book the second before the exam window closes. Both attempts must be used inside the window.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="callout" style={{ marginTop: "1.25rem", borderLeftColor: "#d97706" }}>
      <h3 style={{ margin: "0 0 0.4rem", fontSize: "0.95rem" }}>Before you pay, check six things</h3>
      <p style={{ margin: 0, color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.88rem", lineHeight: 1.75 }}>The exact exam (CKA, CKS or CNPE) · the live price · your country (vouchers are country-locked) · the 6-month redemption deadline · the CKA prerequisite for CKS · that the name on your Linux Foundation account matches your photo ID. Vouchers are non-refundable and non-transferable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout" style={{ marginTop: "1rem" }}>
      <h3 style={{ margin: "0 0 0.4rem", fontSize: "0.95rem" }}>The 6-month rule is the one that bites</h3>
      <p style={{ margin: 0, color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.88rem", lineHeight: 1.75 }}>The Udemy voucher does not start the 12-month exam window until you redeem it. But you must redeem within 6 months of purchase. If you are planning a long study runway, either redeem early and schedule late, or buy direct from the Linux Foundation for a simpler 12-month window.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

