    <h3 style={{ fontSize: "1.05rem", margin: "1.5rem 0 0.5rem" }}>When the Linux Foundation sale beats Udemy</h3>
    <p style={{ color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.92rem", lineHeight: 1.75, margin: "0 0 1rem" }}>
      The Linux Foundation runs promotions throughout the year, especially around Black Friday and Cyber Monday. If a 40%-off sale is live, the $445 exam drops to <strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>$267</strong> — $44.50 below the Udemy price. A 30%-off sale ties Udemy at $311.50. Check the Linux Foundation site on the day you buy; the voucher is a fixed price, not a coupon, so there is no code to stack on top.
    </p>
    <p style={{ color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.9rem", lineHeight: 1.75, margin: 0 }}>
      The bundles are a different calculation. The $625 THRIVE-ONE bundle adds an annual subscription with unlimited e-learning, and the $645 bundle adds a specific course. If you were going to buy training anyway, price the bundle against a discounted Udemy course plus the $311.50 voucher. The voucher alone is still the cheapest way to buy just the exam.
